  "direction": {
    "text": "# General Explainer\n\nTeach one idea from a stable subject: how something works, what the numbers\nsay, how two things differ. Nothing here depends on today's news, so this\nprofile deliberately carries none of the current-affairs rules.\n\n- Open with the question the viewer already has, then answer it once.\n- Facts still need a source when they are specific, but dated sourcing is not\n  required: the subject does not move.\n- Deep blue ground, warm paper panels, a single amber accent for the one\n  number or label that carries the scene.\n- Compare with structure rather than colour: put the two things in the same\n  grid, at the same size, and let the difference show.\n- Motion explains sequence. Reveal in the order the viewer should read, and\n  hold still once everything is on screen.\n",
    "sha256": "76c73e91b14f8da711fc48c27975e579c5306238030708774727522d7fbe5f93"
  }
